1
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:33,440
I'm done studying! I'm done!

2
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:34,480
The questions might know me,

3
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:35,800
but I don't know them!

4
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:37,800
The exam is in a couple of days.

5
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:38,600
Just hang in there.

6
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,400
I have absolutely no hope for college.

7
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:41,840
After I graduate,

8
00:01:41,840 --> 00:01:43,280
I'll just stay at Xiaoxitian.

9
00:01:43,680 --> 00:01:45,880
Funerals are way easier than studying.

10
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:47,600
You need to study

11
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:49,640
with a happy mindset!

12
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:51,000
Don't be so down all the time.

13
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:51,920
Genius Li,

14
00:01:51,920 --> 00:01:53,720
that's easy for you to say.

15
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,920
Studying isn't fun.

16
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:58,320
It's only fun when you actually get it.

17
00:01:58,520 --> 00:01:59,680
As long as you don't regret it.

18
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:01,080
Don't cry later if you fail.

19
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:03,520
We've been studying from dawn to dusk.

20
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,760
How about we play a game?

21
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,080
What game?

22
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:10,840
14, 15, 16.

23
00:02:10,840 --> 00:02:14,760
17, 18, 19, 20.

24
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:17,600
21, 22, 23.

25
00:02:17,600 --> 00:02:19,880
64, 65.

26
00:02:20,080 --> 00:02:21,000
66.

27
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:22,400
This game

28
00:02:22,400 --> 00:02:23,080
is called

29
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:24,080
Destined Encounter.

30
00:02:24,480 --> 00:02:26,960
They say if you leave exactly on the hour

31
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:29,080
and walk 200 steps down the street,

32
00:02:29,360 --> 00:02:30,800
the first person you meet

33
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:32,000
will be your

34
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
destined soulmate for life.

35
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:36,120
What?

36
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:38,720
I'm not playing this childish game with you.

37
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:39,960
Just focus on your exercises.

38
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:42,480
Fine, don't play. Why hit me?

39
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:50,760
Are you getting tired of studying?

40
00:02:51,760 --> 00:02:53,000
I'll go buy two sodas.

41
00:02:53,360 --> 00:02:54,400
As for you, keep working on your exercises.

42
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:55,280
I'll check them when I get back.

43
00:03:02,160 --> 00:03:05,680
121, 122, 123.

44
00:03:05,680 --> 00:03:07,800
124, 125.

45
00:03:08,120 --> 00:03:10,280
156, 157.

46
00:03:10,280 --> 00:03:11,840
158, 159.

47
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:15,200
195, 196, 197.

48
00:03:15,200 --> 00:03:17,360
198, 199.

49
00:03:17,360 --> 00:03:18,160
200.

50
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:27,280
Li Yiran!

51
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:50,520
How many loves can start anew?

52
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:54,400
How many people are worth waiting for?

53
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:59,520
I'll never stop loving, loving, loving you!

54
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:00,480
Wu Huilian.

55
00:04:00,480 --> 00:04:01,440
Are you performing a ritual?

56
00:04:01,440 --> 00:04:02,680
What do you know?

57
00:04:03,080 --> 00:04:03,720
Look,

58
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:05,280
doesn't your mom look stunning today?

59
00:04:05,720 --> 00:04:07,120
Why are you dressed up so provocatively?

60
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:09,800
I'm officially taking clients today.

61
00:04:11,320 --> 00:04:12,480
Let me remind you,

62
00:04:12,680 --> 00:04:13,920
you're going to work,

63
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:15,200
not a beauty pageant.

64
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,920
Dressing so flashy won't do you any good.

65
00:04:17,320 --> 00:04:19,000
Who wants to dress like you young folks?

66
00:04:19,080 --> 00:04:20,880
Wearing baggy clothes all day long.

67
00:04:20,880 --> 00:04:22,520
Going to work looking like you're heading to a funeral.

68
00:04:22,520 --> 00:04:24,560
At work, you need a positive attitude.

69
00:04:24,560 --> 00:04:25,320
Your image

70
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:26,760
should always stay a step ahead of your skills.

71
00:04:26,760 --> 00:04:27,520
Got it?

72
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,640
No, I don't.

73
00:04:30,440 --> 00:04:31,280
Li Yiran.

74
00:04:31,280 --> 00:04:32,840
Today, I, Wu Huilian,

75
00:04:32,840 --> 00:04:35,360
am stepping into a new chapter of my life.

76
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:42,200
I'll never stop loving, loving, loving you!

77
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:45,960
I can wait day by day, month by month, year by year.

78
00:04:45,960 --> 00:04:49,360
Show me your love tonight.

79
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,280
Tonight.

80
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:57,040
Hello, sir.

81
00:04:57,040 --> 00:04:59,080
I'm technician number 33, Lanlan.

82
00:05:04,160 --> 00:05:04,920
Come on.

83
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,480
How am I supposed to wash with water this cold?

84
00:05:07,480 --> 00:05:08,600
Do you use cold water for foot baths at home?

85
00:05:09,280 --> 00:05:11,240
I saw you had such delicate skin,

86
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:12,200
and I didn't want to burn you.

87
00:05:12,200 --> 00:05:13,320
I'm here for a foot wash,

88
00:05:13,320 --> 00:05:14,560
not a facial.

89
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,680
Sorry, sorry.

90
00:05:15,680 --> 00:05:16,480
My apologies.

91
00:05:16,480 --> 00:05:17,760
I'll add some hot water.

92
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:24,600
Adding hot water now.

93
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:29,520
What the hell!

94
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:30,640
Are you trying to scald me to death?

95
00:05:30,640 --> 00:05:31,520
Are you scalding a pig?

96
00:05:37,080 --> 00:05:38,200
What are you looking for?

97
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:40,160
I'm looking for your Baihui acupoint.

98
00:05:44,360 --> 00:05:45,160
Stop, stop, stop.

99
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:46,440
Do you even know how to massage?

100
00:05:46,680 --> 00:05:47,920
I'm new here,

101
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,920
but I can find the Baihui acupoint.

102
00:05:49,920 --> 00:05:51,400
Isn't the Baihui acupoint right here?

103
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,600
I got it.

104
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:53,440
Here we go, sir.

105
00:06:08,400 --> 00:06:09,480
Ma'am.

106
00:06:09,480 --> 00:06:11,160
What are you doing?

107
00:06:11,640 --> 00:06:13,120
Are you kneading dough?

108
00:06:13,840 --> 00:06:14,800
What do you mean?

109
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:16,560
You're not using enough pressure.

110
00:06:17,520 --> 00:06:18,920
What the hell?

111
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:20,680
Press harder, will you!

112
00:06:22,280 --> 00:06:23,000
Got it.

113
00:06:27,360 --> 00:06:29,200
You're crushing my guts!

114
00:06:29,200 --> 00:06:30,280
I'm going to report you!

115
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,200
Get up.

116
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:32,400
Look at her.

117
00:06:36,520 --> 00:06:37,280
Wu Huilian,

118
00:06:37,280 --> 00:06:38,680
you're really something.

119
00:06:39,080 --> 00:06:40,360
Nine complaints in one day.

120
00:06:40,360 --> 00:06:41,720
Why don't you apply for

121
00:06:41,720 --> 00:06:42,800
a Guinness World Record?

122
00:06:43,880 --> 00:06:44,320
I...

123
00:06:44,960 --> 00:06:47,000
I wouldn't win even if I applied.

124
00:06:47,440 --> 00:06:49,920
I heard there was another technician

125
00:06:49,920 --> 00:06:52,160
who got 13 complaints in one day.

126
00:06:52,480 --> 00:06:54,080
Is that something to be proud of?

127
00:06:54,080 --> 00:06:55,280
You're actually comparing yourself?

128
00:06:56,400 --> 00:06:56,920
I...

129
00:06:57,200 --> 00:06:59,200
The customer is God.

130
00:06:59,320 --> 00:07:00,080
God!

131
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:03,080
If I hadn't pleaded with them today,

132
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,600
they'd have canceled their memberships.

133
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:10,640
They're all just bats in chicken feathers,

134
00:07:10,640 --> 00:07:11,320
pretending to be birds.

135
00:07:12,840 --> 00:07:13,640
What did you say?

136
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:17,840
I meant,

137
00:07:17,840 --> 00:07:20,600
the boss's criticism is absolutely right.

138
00:07:20,600 --> 00:07:22,200
I'll definitely correct my mistakes.

139
00:07:24,400 --> 00:07:25,360
You better remember this.

140
00:07:25,960 --> 00:07:27,800
If you get another complaint,

141
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:29,280
you can pack your bags

142
00:07:29,280 --> 00:07:29,920
and get out.

143
00:07:40,280 --> 00:07:41,280
This grass

144
00:07:41,800 --> 00:07:42,960
is really expensive.

145
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:52,680
Grass?

146
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,640
What kind of grass are you?

147
00:07:55,120 --> 00:07:56,080
How expensive can you be?

148
00:07:56,360 --> 00:07:58,640
I'm going to rip you to shreds!

149
00:08:03,520 --> 00:08:05,200
Why are you still laughing?

150
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,080
Shiqi,

151
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:10,440
I've set you up with Director Wang's son.

152
00:08:10,640 --> 00:08:11,720
Today at noon,

153
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:12,800
you're going to have lunch together.

154
00:08:15,280 --> 00:08:15,960
Dad,

155
00:08:16,480 --> 00:08:17,280
how could you arrange this

156
00:08:17,280 --> 00:08:18,520
without even asking me?

157
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:19,720
Shiqi,

158
00:08:19,880 --> 00:08:21,800
it won't hurt to just meet him.

159
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:22,760
What if you two hit it off?

160
00:08:23,640 --> 00:08:24,920
Didn't we agree

161
00:08:24,920 --> 00:08:26,720
that my love life is my own decision?

162
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:28,480
Your dad has already made the plans.

163
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:30,560
We have to show respect to Director Wang.

164
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,480
Then why should I be the one to do it?

165
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,600
If he wants to climb the social ladder,

166
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:36,120
let him show respect himself!

167
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:37,920
You're a grown woman.

168
00:08:38,160 --> 00:08:39,480
Do you have any idea

169
00:08:39,480 --> 00:08:41,640
how hard it is to find someone

170
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:42,520
of equal social standing for you?

171
00:08:42,920 --> 00:08:44,880
And you insist on making your own choices,

172
00:08:44,880 --> 00:08:46,960
just to be with some undertaker?

173
00:08:46,960 --> 00:08:48,240
What's wrong with being an undertaker?

174
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:50,480
Even if Chen Baixi has no money,

175
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:51,960
I'm willing to struggle alongside him!

176
00:08:52,760 --> 00:08:53,720
Marriage

177
00:08:53,920 --> 00:08:55,000
is about two families,

178
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,480
not just two people.

179
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:58,800
You're going today whether you like it or not!

180
00:09:00,120 --> 00:09:00,880
Lao Fan!

181
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:02,800
You really are...

182
00:09:02,800 --> 00:09:04,560
Lao Fan! Lao Fan!

183
00:09:18,160 --> 00:09:19,680
Look how thin you are.

184
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:20,640
Eat some more.

185
00:09:22,360 --> 00:09:23,120
I'm not hungry.

186
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:26,680
Is the food I ordered for you

187
00:09:26,680 --> 00:09:27,720
not to your liking?

188
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:29,720
What would you like to eat?

189
00:09:30,600 --> 00:09:32,160
Should we go to another restaurant?

190
00:09:32,560 --> 00:09:33,520
Don't go to the trouble.

191
00:09:33,520 --> 00:09:34,680
I'm really not hungry.

192
00:09:44,880 --> 00:09:47,080
This is a gift I got for you.

193
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:48,640
See if you like it.

194
00:09:49,560 --> 00:09:50,600
It's too expensive.

195
00:09:50,600 --> 00:09:51,360
I can't accept it.

196
00:09:52,080 --> 00:09:53,360
It didn't cost much.

197
00:09:53,360 --> 00:09:54,200
Most importantly,

198
00:09:54,880 --> 00:09:56,240
I'm quite satisfied with you.

199
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:58,000
After you marry into my family,

200
00:09:58,000 --> 00:09:59,440
you'll quit that dead-end job.

201
00:09:59,480 --> 00:10:00,640
My family doesn't like women

202
00:10:00,640 --> 00:10:01,960
showing their faces in public.

203
00:10:02,720 --> 00:10:04,000
You'll just stay home and have kids.

204
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:04,840
And raise them.

205
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:06,720
Ideally, both a boy and a girl.

206
00:10:06,720 --> 00:10:07,840
You mean

207
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:10,040
you want me to be a full-time housewife?

208
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:11,080
Exactly.

209
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:12,240
When you marry into our family,

210
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:14,000
you have to follow our rules.

211
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,960
So I'll stay home, support my husband, raise the kids,

212
00:10:15,960 --> 00:10:16,680
serve my in-laws,

213
00:10:16,680 --> 00:10:17,280
and do all the chores.

214
00:10:17,280 --> 00:10:18,200
Is that what you mean?

215
00:10:18,320 --> 00:10:19,360
That's right.

216
00:10:19,360 --> 00:10:20,520
I didn't expect you to be so understanding.

217
00:10:20,520 --> 00:10:21,040
Yeah.

218
00:10:21,040 --> 00:10:22,520
I didn't expect you to be so amusing.

219
00:10:29,680 --> 00:10:30,440
Excuse me,

220
00:10:30,440 --> 00:10:31,440
something came up at work.

221
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:32,600
I have to go.

222
00:10:33,080 --> 00:10:33,880
Let me give you a ride.

223
00:10:34,960 --> 00:10:36,040
Let me drive you, Shiqi.

224
00:10:39,360 --> 00:10:41,000
Shiqi, wait for me!

225
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:41,720
Shiqi!

226
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:44,040
Shiqi, slow down! Wait for me!

227
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:48,000
Shiqi, where are you going? I'll drive you!

228
00:10:49,800 --> 00:10:51,160
No need. It's out of your way.

229
00:10:52,480 --> 00:10:53,600
Let me drive you.

230
00:10:53,600 --> 00:10:54,600
Don't embarrass me.

231
00:10:56,800 --> 00:10:57,760
I said I don't need a ride.

232
00:10:59,440 --> 00:11:00,280
I said I don't need a ride!

233
00:11:00,280 --> 00:11:01,000
What are you doing?

234
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:02,600
Let her go.

235
00:11:04,080 --> 00:11:05,320
She already said she doesn't need it.

236
00:11:05,600 --> 00:11:07,200
Who are you? Mind your own business.

237
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,160
Bullying a girl in broad daylight...

238
00:11:10,400 --> 00:11:11,280
Have you no shame?

239
00:11:12,480 --> 00:11:13,800
Shiqi, do you know him?

240
00:11:14,560 --> 00:11:15,680
More than just know him.

241
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:16,640
I am her...

242
00:11:16,640 --> 00:11:17,720
He's my boyfriend.

243
00:11:21,680 --> 00:11:23,200
You're on a blind date when you have a boyfriend?

244
00:11:23,360 --> 00:11:24,600
Are you messing with me?

245
00:11:25,200 --> 00:11:26,600
You, and you!

246
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:27,560
Just you wait!

247
00:11:29,920 --> 00:11:31,440
Yeah, right. What a jerk.

248
00:11:39,880 --> 00:11:41,040
Are you okay?

249
00:11:42,160 --> 00:11:43,000
I'm fine.

250
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:45,000
What a creep.

251
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
So classless.

252
00:11:46,120 --> 00:11:47,480
That was a blind date arranged by my family.

253
00:11:47,480 --> 00:11:48,600
I don't like him at all.

254
00:11:55,360 --> 00:11:56,680
I just finished a business meeting.

255
00:11:56,680 --> 00:11:57,680
My car is over there.

256
00:11:58,040 --> 00:11:59,160
How about I give you a ride back?

257
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:00,360
Okay.

258
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:02,480
Let's go.

259
00:12:08,880 --> 00:12:09,560
By the way,

260
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:10,880
what did you want to see me about last time?

261
00:12:13,320 --> 00:12:15,360
That feature on young people returning from big cities...

262
00:12:15,360 --> 00:12:17,000
We might have to put it on hold for now.

263
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,400
The station has adjusted its direction.

264
00:12:19,400 --> 00:12:21,240
They want to focus on social hot topics.

265
00:12:21,480 --> 00:12:24,160
Returning youths is definitely a topic worth covering.

266
00:12:24,160 --> 00:12:26,320
But maybe it's not the right time.

267
00:12:28,720 --> 00:12:30,520
Actually, there are many young people right now

268
00:12:30,520 --> 00:12:32,080
who choose to escape the big cities

269
00:12:32,880 --> 00:12:33,880
and return to their hometowns.

270
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:35,760
It's already become a phenomenon.

271
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:38,000
It would be a good thing to report on it.

272
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:40,720
It's the station's decision.

273
00:12:43,800 --> 00:12:45,200
I know it's not yours.

274
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,520
You look a little tired.

275
00:12:52,520 --> 00:12:53,720
You need to take care of yourself.

276
00:12:55,320 --> 00:12:58,160
Work hasn't been going too well lately.

277
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,520
Well, that's work.

278
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:02,920
There will always be rough times.

279
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:05,440
But I believe...

280
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,400
...you're so talented.

281
00:13:06,920 --> 00:13:07,840
You'll do just fine.

282
00:13:11,520 --> 00:13:13,560
Thank you, Chen Baixi.

283
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:18,320
You're right.

284
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:19,960
I'll keep working hard.

285
00:13:20,560 --> 00:13:22,400
I need to prove myself to them.

286
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:24,360
You can do it.

287
